{
	"_source": "The ghost's cutout rig (Phase 3, 2026-11-21; docs/art/characters/GHOST.md §7). Canvas px of the 1024 × 1024 generated images on flat mid-grey (cut with bg_min 0.6). Sources: ref_* = the approved references with the painted glow removed by an edit (the game draws its own glow); rig_front / rig_back = the arms angled out so they cut clean; base_side = the side view with the near arm removed by an edit (its legs are cut off by the polygon); part_side_arm / part_side_legs = the near arm and both legs alone. Front and back: head, body, two arms and two whole legs (hip to boot: the legs hang, so they swing from the hip; knees are not split). Side (facing right; left is mirrored): head, body, the near arm, one legs part (separate near/far legs could not be generated: the edits returned the whole figure). Arms are painted 25° out: the clips hold them 9–12° in. The figure is 923 px from hair to the lowest toe ≈ 1.80 m hanging (he is about 1.78 m standing): 510 px per metre. The foot point is the floor point under him, 'hover_m' below his lowest toe. Build: python3 tools/art/rig_build.py ghost. Clips: Keys [t, rot°, dx, dy, sy] per part (canvas px × 0.4). Positive rotation is clockwise on screen: a front left arm (viewer's left) swings out with +, a right arm with −; in the side view (facing right) + leans the body forward and swings the legs and arm back. Lean, the legs' trailing and their settle are added on top by GhostAnimator from the ghost's real speed; these clips carry the breathing, the bob and the gestures. Wash (2026-11-21, in-game review): the back view was generated ~15 % darker and the side greyer than the canonical front; their non-ink pixels are washed toward pale icy blue (back 0.2, side 0.1) by tools/art/wash.gd at build time; the front is untouched. Scale (2026-11-21, user review \"bigger than the father\"): the family is drawn at the storybook scale ~0.76 of nominal height (father 1.85 m → 1.42 m figure); the ghost follows it — 933 px figure = 1.38 m (676 px per metre), hover 0.16 m.",
